{"id":"n-20261008-5u6iuu","category":"sports","display_title":"Kerem Primo Wins World Silver","display_title_he":"כרם פרימו זכתה במדליית כסף עולמית","short_summary":"Israeli judoka Kerem Primo secured a silver medal at the World Judo Championships in Baku after an impressive run, surpassing initial expectations.","english_level":"C1","words":442,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Walla","domain":"sports.walla.co.il","url":"https://sports.walla.co.il/item/3871348","title":"בנבחרת בנו על אשפיז והרשקו, אבל אז הופיעה כרם פרימו","published_at":"2026-10-08T09:02:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-08T09:02:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-08T06:20:32.412Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The Israeli delegation participating in the World Judo Championships in Baku experienced a mix of heavy disappointment and unexpected elation. Prior to the opening of the premier international competition, the largest gathering for the national judo team since the Paris Olympic Games held more than two years ago, officials within the delegation had primarily focused their medal expectations on two distinct athletes: Yitzhak Ashpiz in the men's division and Raz Hershko in the women's weight classes.","The initial days of the tournament did not go according to the anticipated script. Ashpiz, competing in the under-60 kilogram weight class, opened the competition in the capital of Azerbaijan. Attention centered on this eighteen-year-old talent from Rishon LeZion, who was accustomed to winning and genuinely believed he could stand on the podium despite his youth. Both the athlete and the Israel Judo Association were fully convinced of his capabilities. However, Ashpiz suffered a surprising defeat in his very first bout, resulting in an immediate exit from the competition.","Further setbacks followed as the tournament progressed. Timna Nelson Levy missed out on the podium in the under-57 kilogram category, failing to reach the top despite being capable of achieving it on a good day. Among the sisters Gefen and Kerem Primo, expectations had actually pointed toward the older sister, Gefen, but she was unable to advance toward medal contention.","However, the narrative shifted dramatically when twenty-one-year-old Kerem Primo began her remarkable campaign. She advanced steadily through the rounds until she reached the final match, where she faced the formidable Japanese world champion, Haruka Kaju. Delegation members noted that overcoming Kaju demands an extraordinary performance from the challenger alongside a notably less stellar performance from Kaju herself. Team staff inside the camp in Baku remarked that not being crowned world champion after losing a final match specifically to Kaju feels precisely like taking the world championship itself.","Staff enthusiastically praised her exceptional level of judo, describing her as a true fighter and highlighting the immense resilience required to reach a world championship final at such a young age, particularly after enduring serious physical setbacks, surgeries, and a torn cruciate ligament in her knee that sidelined her for a grueling year and a half. Officials emphasized that her phenomenal success significantly broadens the depth and potential of the women's national team, proving there is currently a great deal to offer within the women's squad. While other judokas still had matches ahead until the conclusion of the tournament, it was evident that the focus of everyone in the delegation had now turned toward Raz Hershko, who was fully capable of finishing the championship for Israel as a world champion."],"facts":[{"fact":"Kerem Primo won a silver medal at the World Judo Championships in Baku.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Primo lost in the final to Japanese world champion Haruka Kaju.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Before the tournament, the Israeli delegation pinned its main medal hopes on Yitzhak Ashpiz and Raz Hershko.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Ashpiz was eliminated in his very first match.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Primo's achievement comes after a year and a half absence due to a torn cruciate ligament and subsequent surgeries.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Gefen Primo and Timna Nelson Levy did not reach the podium.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Israeli","lemma":"Israeli","pos":"adj","he":"ישראלי","name":"false"},{"text":"delegation","lemma":"delegation","pos":"noun","he":"משלחת","name":false},{"text":"participating","lemma":"participate","pos":"verb","he":"משתתף","name":false},{"text":"World Judo Championships","lemma":"World Judo Championships","pos":"noun","he":"אליפות העולם בג'ודו","name":"true"},{"text":"Baku","lemma":"Baku","pos":"noun","he":"באקו","name":"true"},{"text":"experienced","lemma":"experience","pos":"verb","he":"חווה","name":false},{"text":"mix","lemma":"mix","pos":"noun","he":"תערובת","name":false},{"text":"heavy","lemma":"heavy","pos":"adj","he":"כבד","name":false},{"text":"disappointment","lemma":"disappointment","pos":"noun","he":"אכזבה","name":false},{"text":"unexpected","lemma":"unexpected","pos":"adj","he":"בלתי צפוי","name":false},{"text":"elation","lemma":"elation","pos":"noun","he":"שמחה, הקלה","name":false},{"text":"Prior","lemma":"prior","pos":"prep","he":"ערב, לפני","name":"false"},{"text":"opening","lemma":"opening","pos":"noun","he":"פתיחה","name":false},{"text":"premier","lemma":"premier","pos":"adj","he":"ראשי, הגדול ביותר","name":false},{"text":"international","lemma":"international","pos":"adj","he":"בינלאומי","name":false},{"text":"competition","lemma":"competition","pos":"noun","he":"תחרות","name":false},{"text":"largest","lemma":"large","pos":"adj","he":"הגדול ביותר","name":false},{"text":"gathering","lemma":"gathering","pos":"noun","he":"אירוע, כינוס","name":false},{"text":"national","lemma":"national","pos":"adj","he":"לאומי","name":false},{"text":"judo","lemma":"judo","pos":"noun","he":"ג'ודו","name":false},{"text":"tea